BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (The first money trap is invisible books. Jesse Vasquez admits all early cash went into one place and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (profitability was unknown, relays CPA Amanda Han's warning that commingled funds get traced back to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (personal accounts in a lawsuit, and says the business operated blind on bookkeeping for five to six years) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (before Baselane sub-accounts fixed it [NTumQCcmf3s @ 00:02:18]. The second trap is bad Coverage D) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (math. Ruben Kanya warns that land value must be stripped first: a $1.2M California home can carry) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm ($600-700K of land and only a $300K dwelling, and in the Smyrna example a $480K buy minus about 10%) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (land left a $432K dwelling, so 20% equals $86,400, or $7,200 a month over 12 months [vbHlGVZKjvg @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (00:44:11]. Insurers also push back with "running out of money" while the policy says unlimited. Wording) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (before the claim call matters too: the claim is on the leak, not the mold, and "flood" versus "leak" decides) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (eligibility, which is why Ruben pushes a public adjuster and cites a $2,000 claim that became $20,000) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm ([g075AOuQIwk @ 00:25:28]. Shona's napkin version, 20-25% of dwelling value, carries the same caveat) Tj ET
