BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 224.87 Tm (out of town, the trip was denied, and because the hotel was still being paid while they were away, they) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 209.65 Tm (arguably owe that money back [awTD63In04A @ 00:12:29]. Trishaan's lesson is to ask about trips at the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 194.42 Tm (very start, because it is better to have that conversation in the beginning than to argue about it on the back) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 179.20 Tm (end. Mike Crowley sets the same ceiling from the agency side: carriers move big losses into a rented house) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 163.97 Tm (or apartment, and there is no milking a five-star hotel [TkI2Qak3r34 @ 00:01:47]. The furnished alternative) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 148.75 Tm (looks like Gng. Jackson's employer-provided unit: fully stocked, a new washer and dryer, kids' beds,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 133.53 Tm (welcome food, pet gifts and a gate code [hp6VgBcT7YQ @ 00:04:16].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 118.30 Tm (The second trap is the baseline. Bill Coffman's formula is total expenses minus normal expenses, and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 103.08 Tm (warning is blunt: if you overestimate your normal expenses, you get shortchanged on your recovery) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 87.85 Tm ([idtxFNBKKIA @ 00:01:27]. Kela Trishaan shows how the adjuster builds that baseline: groceries of $150 to) Tj ET
